course: dictionary
lesson: 4528
title: Headwinds and hard going
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A headwind is a wind that blows straight at you, against the way you are going, so it slows you down. «The cyclists rode into a strong headwind» tells you the wind was pushing back at them, so they went more slowly.
explain: Words can also be used in a picture sense. «Headwinds» in business means problems that hurt sales. Businesses do not feel real wind, so ask what would fit: problems that make progress harder. Swap that meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: A tailwind is the opposite. It blows from behind and helps you go faster. When you meet a new word, look for its opposite in the lesson or the text, because the opposite often shows you what the word means.
fact: A headwind is a wind blowing straight towards you, against the way you are going.
fact: A headwind slows a plane, boat or cyclist down.
fact: A tailwind blows from behind and adds to your speed.
fact: «Headwinds» can also mean something that makes progress harder, such as problems in business.
fact: Phrases to know: «a strong headwind», «into a headwind», «face headwinds».
exercise: «The plane flew into a strong headwind, so it was slower.» What is a headwind? | A cool breeze at the seaside | A wind blowing behind you that helps you go faster | *A wind blowing straight at you, against your direction | A storm with lots of rain
exercise: «The business faced headwinds.» What does headwinds mean here? | Gifts from happy customers | Sales that went up very quickly | Strong winds that blew the shop sign down | *Problems that make progress harder
exercise: Which wind would slow a cyclist down? | A gentle wind that does not move | A warm wind that smells of flowers | *A headwind, which blows straight at her | A tailwind, which pushes from behind
test: «The team had to face headwinds all season.» What does this suggest? | The team's wind was from behind | *The team found things hard and progress was difficult | The team won every game easily | The team had a holiday
test: What is the opposite of a headwind? | A cold wind | *A tailwind | A calm sea | A dark cloud
exam: Maya says a headwind is only about weather. Is she right? | *No, it can also mean problems that make progress harder | Yes, a headwind is only ever about wind | Yes, but only in winter | No, a headwind is a kind of boat
